# Licensing / 授權

This repository is dual-licensed. Which licence applies depends on which part
of the repository the material comes from.

本專案採雙授權。適用哪一種授權，取決於材料位於本專案的哪個部分。

## 1. Prose, teaching material, and documentation — CC BY-SA 4.0

Applies to: `*.qmd`, `*.md` (including `README.md` and `PROPOSAL.zh-TW.md`),
and any rendered output derived from them under `docs/`.

適用於：`*.qmd`、`*.md`（含 `README.md` 與 `PROPOSAL.zh-TW.md`），
以及 `docs/` 底下由這些檔案產生的網頁輸出。

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
Licence (CC BY-SA 4.0). Full legal code:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Rationale: ShareAlike keeps the option open to adapt passages from the external
teaching material this project links to (psyteachr, lsj-book), which is itself
mostly CC BY-SA 4.0.

理由：保留日後改寫本專案所連結之外部教材（psyteachr、lsj-book，多為
CC BY-SA 4.0）段落的餘地。

## 2. Prompt entries, schema, and code — MIT

Applies to: `prompts/_schema.yaml`, `prompts/entries/*.yaml`, `tools/*.R`,
`tests/**`, `_quarto.yml`, `_quarto-en.yml`, and `docs/prompts.json`.

適用於：`prompts/_schema.yaml`、`prompts/entries/*.yaml`、`tools/*.R`、
`tests/**`、`_quarto.yml`、`_quarto-en.yml`、`docs/prompts.json`。

Rationale: users copy prompts into jamovi and adapt them for their own data.
They should not incur an attribution or share-alike obligation for doing so.

理由：使用者會把提示詞複製進 jamovi 並依自己的資料改寫，不該因此背負
署名或相同方式分享的義務。

